<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Choose two transformations so that the first followed by the second has the same effect as the reflection in the y-axis. The first transformation must be a rotation.</p><div>First: [ reflection in the x-axis | reflection in the y-axis | reflection in the line y = x | reflection in the line y = −x | rotation of 90° anticlockwise about O | rotation of 180° about O | rotation of 90° clockwise about O ] </div><div>Second: [ reflection in the x-axis | reflection in the y-axis | reflection in the line y = x | reflection in the line y = −x | rotation of 90° anticlockwise about O | rotation of 180° about O | rotation of 90° clockwise about O ] </div><div/></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The matrix of the reflection in the y-axis is <m>{\left[\begin{array}{cc} -1 &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; 1 \end{array}\right]}</m>. For a pair to work, (second) <m>\times</m> (first) must equal it, and the first must be a rotation.</p><p>One pair that works: the rotation of <m>90^\circ</m> anticlockwise about O followed by the reflection in the line <m>y = -x</m>, since <m>{\left[\begin{array}{cc} 0 &amp; -1 \\ -1 &amp; 0 \end{array}\right]}{\left[\begin{array}{cc} 0 &amp; -1 \\ 1 &amp; 0 \end{array}\right]} = {\left[\begin{array}{cc} -1 &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; 1 \end{array}\right]}</m>. Another: the rotation of <m>180^\circ</m> about O followed by the reflection in the x-axis.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p>rotation of 90° anticlockwise about O</p></answer>
    <answer><p>reflection in the line y = −x</p></answer>
</stack-static>